# Everything here is excluded from the build context -- the tarball Docker
# ships to the daemon before running a single instruction. data/ alone is
# ~14,000 files; sending it would slow every build and it is never used at
# inference time.
#
# This file is also a correctness control, not just a speed one: anything not
# excluded can be silently baked into an image layer by a broad `COPY . .`,
# including .env files and credentials.

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

data/
docs/
*.md
!README.md

.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Training-only artifacts. The image needs head.pt and nothing else from here;
# history/eval JSON are development records.
artifacts/*.history.json
artifacts/eval-*.json
artifacts/linear.pt
